Project Todo List – Master
Includes all tasks from the original list, the detailed bullet points, and the new directives (merged packages, Docker env consolidation, error fixing, testing, agents, docs, and component enhancements).

0. Global Pre‑Requisites
Confirmed applications/libs/ref was removed after package merge
Merge its two packages fully into:

applications/libs/django-osoul

applications/libs/crafts-ai
with all content, code, and logic organised and no remaining references to ref.

Solve all errors in ctc-research/gunicorn-error.log
Redeploy and run the project locally, execute the full test suite, and make sure all tests pass and all issues are resolved.

Fix any import errors that may appear (even if not yet visible).

1. Docker & Configuration
Consolidate Docker environment variables
In every docker‑compose file, create a site-env (or x-env) section that contains all configuration from the corresponding .env files. This keeps containers lightweight and easy to read.

Verify all relative paths in Docker Compose (especially VResume)
Point them to the central applications/ directory structure.

Docker container env vars & passwords
Check that all passwords are correctly linked across services, and that all make commands and service delegations (in docker/makefile at ../services) work for deployments.

Fix mount points and config copying

Mount configs, CLI, and commands from the main applications/ directory instead of copying per‑website (ctc-research, vresume, lms-demo).

Ensure lms-demo assets and ctc-research configs are properly linked/copied from applications/.

Logs directory

Logs must be website‑specific (no sharing).

The shared logs directory under applications/ should have daily‑updated names.

Implement make commands to clean up logs (both per‑site and global).

2. Template & SCSS – BEM Customization (MCP/AI tasks)
Wagtail admin customisation
Apply the static styles from applications/assets/static/styles (same colours as the main website).

Merge duplicated templates
Combine them into single, fully optimised templates that share the same styles.

Update lms-demo assets/styles to meet BEM requirements.

Theme conversion

Copy the latest theme styles and convert them to BEM format.

After conversion, update the corresponding components.

Integrate AI / Crafts file tasks with .kilo/mcp_server.py

Analyse the theme directory with the MCP server.

Map components to the appropriate websites.

Replace the components with the correct Django tags, adding necessary data.

Update the styles of applications/lms-demo/assets/static/styles accordingly.

3. Accounts / Auth
Refactor plugins/accounts/allauth_views.py
Move it to plugins/accounts/views/ and split it into separate, named files.

Management files
Verify that all files moved in the last commit can still be imported from their old paths (e.g. accounts or accounts/registration). Update any imports that broke.

Auth templates relocation

Update any templates that were moved from auth to account.

Make the sign‑in page match the login template and reuse the fragment‑loaded page_auth layout.

Enhance allauth / htmx integration
Both fragmented htmx auth pages must use the same mechanism and functionality.
If the request is not an htmx request, fall back gracefully to a normal full‑page request.

4. Template Organization
Centralise templates/components
The base location is applications/assets/templates.
All organised components, comp tags, and OOP components must be placed there.

Remove duplicated files
Delete any duplicates from vresume and lms-demo – they must use the centralised versions under ctc-research.

Fix all template paths for components, {% comp %} tags, and OOP components.

Update lms-demo templates to match the ctc-research structure.

Ensure structural consistency across all websites (vresume, lms-demo)
Any file that now exists in the base assets directory should be removed from website‑specific directories, and all references must be updated.

5. Library Merge & Code Organisation
Merged django-osoul compatibility plan → final location: applications/libs/django-osoul

Merged crafts-ai compatibility plan → final location: applications/libs/crafts-ai

Check for duplicated configurations
If any component or configuration from crafts-ai already exists in django-osoul, consolidate them into django-osoul.

Organise directories and namespaces
Use effective, use‑case‑based names, and follow Django conventions (contrib, models, managers, management/services, etc.).

Update all imports across every website
Any references to the old rseal or grep packages must be corrected.

6. Post‑Merge Enhancements & Recommendations
Once libraries are merged and tests pass:

Write a recommendations document (agents.md)

Describe how to enhance django-osoul and crafts-ai using .kilo files and the MCP server.

Include guidelines for customising designs across all websites.

Ensure the todo list itself remains aware of these enhancements.

Generate agent configurations

Create agents at template paths and model paths.

For any component templates that are part of django-osoul, move them to assets/templates and merge properly.

Add a markdown file detailing the enhancements and proposed new features.

Enhance documentation
Improve the full project documentation to reflect the new merged structure and all recent changes.

Test the merged packages

Run all tests after merging.

Add cache enhancements to django-osoul — create base classes for managers and caches similar to what is already in ctc-research.

Enhance component tags

Fix any errors that appear in component rendering.

Integrate components with viewsets and with the OOP components.

Document the full featured usage.

Add error logging to the component system:

Track where an HTML file is rendered.

Log any context errors that occur.

Implement a loader/fallback mechanism – if the main response takes too long, show a loader for the same component before the final response.

7. Testing & Final Verification
Solve all errors from ctc-research/gunicorn-error.log.

Run the full test suite locally and ensure every test passes.

Fix any remaining import errors across all websites.

Re‑deploy and confirm everything works end‑to‑end.

